# health v2.9 — WARNING. "sensitivity" written to clinical:allergyType.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT VALUE. FHIR R4 AllergyIntolerance.type has a REQUIRED binding
# to exactly two codes, allergy | intolerance, and "sensitivity" is the word a
# patient portal or an intake form routinely prints for both of them. It is not
# a typo and not gibberish: it is the plausible third word, the one a converter
# would pass through unexamined because it reads as a synonym, and the one that
# collapses the distinction the element exists to make. An immune-mediated
# allergy and a non-immune intolerance are different mechanisms with different
# consequences, and a record that says "sensitivity" has stated neither.
#
# The other reason for this value rather than a two-code near-miss: the set has
# only two members, so any fixture at all proves the binding is enumerated. What
# a plausible third word proves additionally is that the binding was narrowed to
# two BY the FHIR required binding rather than by an author who did not think of
# a third case.
#
# sh:Warning, not sh:Violation, per the core v3.5 ratchet: this is the first
# release to bind clinical:allergyType on any shape. Nothing rejects this
# record, and the fixture asserts exactly that alongside the warning.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:a11e0209-0000-4000-8000-000000000003> a health:AllergyRecord ;
    health:allergen "Lactose" ;
    health:allergenCode <http://snomed.info/sct/47703008> ;
    health:allergyCategory "food" ;
    health:reaction "Abdominal bloating" ;
    clinical:allergyType "sensitivity" ;
    clinical:status "active" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
